.TH HD-LAUNCHER-CACHE 1 "October 2026" "hd-desktop" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-launcher-cache \- write and print the menu of the application launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-launcher-cache
.br
.B hd-launcher-cache
.BR \-u | \-\-update
.br
.B hd-launcher-cache
.BR \-a | \-\-update\-all
.br
.B hd-launcher-cache
.BR \-n | \-\-dry\-run
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-launcher-cache
writes the menu of the application launcher of the HyprDebian desktop, the
input of
.BR hd-menu (1),
in a cache, from the
.I .desktop
files in
.I /usr/share/applications
and its subdirectories, and the key
.B hd-launcher
of the configuration (see CONFIGURATION).
Without arguments, it prints the menu for the launcher.
.PP
Who runs it decides which settings and which cache it uses.
Root uses the configuration of the system,
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
and the cache of the system,
.IR /var/cache/hd-launcher .
Any other user uses the keys
.B hd-launcher
and
.B hd-theme
of their own configuration,
.IR ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json ,
when it has them, else those of the configuration of the system, and their
own cache,
.IR ~/.cache/hd-launcher .
.PP
Without arguments, it prints the menu in the cache of the user, else the one
in the cache of the system.
When neither cache has a menu, it prints a menu with the single option
.B No cache
and a warning icon, which does nothing when chosen.
Root only looks in the cache of the system.
The key binding of the launcher in
.I ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua
pipes it into
.BR hd-menu .
.PP
An application is in the menu when its
.I .desktop
file is of the
.B Type
Application, has a
.B Name
and an
.BR Exec ,
is not
.B NoDisplay
or
.BR Hidden ,
is not left out for Hyprland by
.B OnlyShowIn
or
.BR NotShowIn ,
has its
.B TryExec
installed, when it has one, and is not left out by the key
.B hd-launcher
(see CONFIGURATION).
.PP
The menu is 40% of the width and the height of the output; the options that
do not fit scroll.
Every application and every item added is an option, with its
.B Name
or
.B name
as the label.
The value is the command line that starts it as a systemd user unit of its
own, quoted for the shell, which the launcher runs with
.BR "sh \-c" :
.B uwsm app \-\-
with the desktop file ID of an application, such as
.IR firefox.desktop ,
or the command of an item added.
The ID of a file in a subdirectory is its path below
.I /usr/share/applications
with \- for /.
The options are sorted on the label, in ascending order, without regard to
case.
.PP
The icon of an application is looked up by its
.B Icon
in the icon themes hicolor and Adwaita and in
.IR /usr/share/pixmaps ,
or taken from its path when it is one.
A PNG is used as it is.
An SVG is rendered to a PNG of the
.B icon_size
of the
.BR hd-theme ,
64 without one, in
.I icons
of the cache; only when the PNG there was not rendered from that SVG at that size.
The icons of applications that are gone or left out are removed.
.PP
The apt hook
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/90hd-launcher
runs
.B hd-launcher-cache \-\-update\-all
as root each time apt has run dpkg: after an installation, an upgrade or a
removal, so the menus of the system and of the users in the group
.B users
follow the applications.
A failure is reported but does not fail apt.
The installation of
.BR hd-desktop (7)
runs it too.
The cache of a user who is not in the group
.B users
is only written when that user runs
.BR "hd-launcher-cache \-\-update" .
After another theme is selected, with another
.BR icon_size ,
or after the settings changed, run it again.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ,\  \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-u ,\  \-\-update
Write the menu and its icons in the cache: of the system for root, of the
user for other users.
.TP
.BR \-a ,\  \-\-update\-all
Run as root only: write the cache of the system, then run
.B hd-launcher-cache \-\-update
with
.BR runuser (1)
as each user whose primary or supplementary group is
.B users
and whose home directory exists, so each cache belongs to its user and is
made from the settings of that user.
A user whose cache cannot be written is reported, the others are still
written, and the exit status is 1.
.TP
.BR \-n ,\  \-\-dry\-run
Print the menu that
.B \-\-update
would write, write nothing.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The key
.B hd-launcher
of the configuration leaves applications out of the menu and adds items of its own:
.PP
.RS
.nf
"hd-launcher": {
    "exclude": ["org.gnome.Meld.desktop", "debian-xterm"],
    "add": [
        {
            "name": "Btop",
            "command": ["kitty", "\-e", "btop"],
            "icon": "utilities-system-monitor"
        }
    ]
}
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B exclude
Optional: the desktop file IDs to leave out; the
.I .desktop
at the end may be left out.
.TP
.B add
Optional: the items to add, each an object with:
.RS
.TP
.B name
The label.
.TP
.B command
The words of the command, a list of strings, run without a shell.
For pipes, variables or
.IR ~ ,
use
.BR "[\(dqsh\(dq, \(dq\-c\(dq, \(dq...\(dq]" .
.TP
.B icon
Optional: the path of a PNG or SVG, or the name of an icon, looked up as the
.B Icon
of an application.
An icon that is not found is reported and left out.
.RE
.PP
Other members, or a key that is not such an object, are an error: the menu
is not written.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/cache/hd-launcher/launcher.json
.TQ
.I ~/.cache/hd-launcher/launcher.json
The menu, for
.BR hd-menu (1),
of the system and of the user.
.TP
.I /var/cache/hd-launcher/icons
.TQ
.I ~/.cache/hd-launcher/icons
The PNGs rendered from SVG icons.
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-desktop/icons/warning.svg
The icon of the menu without a cache.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/90hd-launcher
The apt hook.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
.TQ
.I ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json
The configuration of the system and of the user: the applications to leave
out and the items to add, in the key
.BR hd-launcher ,
and the
.BR icon_size ,
in the key
.BR hd-theme .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the menu was written or printed, 1 on an error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-desktop (7),
.BR hd-menu (1),
.BR hd-theme (7),
.BR hd-config (7)
